<title>JAPAN: Daiichikosho says to post Y1.84 bln special profit.</title>
<headline>Daiichikosho says to post Y1.84 bln special profit.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daiichikosho Co Ltd said on Tuesday it would post a special profit of 1.84 billion yen after selling a Boeing 737 it had bought for investment purposes.</p>
<p>The plane was sold last month to Bbam Aircraft Holdings Nine Ltd, an aircraft company located in the Cayman Islands, for $19.84 million, it said.</p>
<p>Despite the special profit, Daiichikosho said in a statement it would not change its earnings forecast for the full business year to March 31 because it expects losses resulting from planned sales or removal of its fixed asset holdings in the latter half of the year.</p>
<p>The company sells and leases karaoke equipment in Japan.</p>
</text>
